---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { workflowSections } from '../lib/workflow';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="DFT Research Workflow"
  description="A software-neutral guide to researcher-scale DFT tasks, target calculations, validation, and reproducibility."
  current="home"
>
  <h1>DFT Research Workflow</h1>
  <p class="home-intro">
    DFT Research Workflow explains how researchers move from a material structure to interpretable, validated, and reproducible results. The site follows five broad parts: Structures, Calculation Preparation, Reference-State Calculations, Target Calculations, and Research Completion. These parts are a branching and revisitable learning map, not a claim that every study follows one fixed sequence. A result can send the researcher back to the structure, method, reference state, or convergence design. Target calculations form a library: band structures, density of states, phonons, defects, transport, optical response, electron–phonon coupling, superconductivity, and other calculations are distinct scientific tasks when their methods and evidence differ. Start with the <a href={withBase('operations/')}>Research Workflow</a>, then inspect <a href={withBase('workflows/')}>Worked Workflows</a> whose commands, outputs, checks, parsers, tables, and figures come from published case directories.
  </p>

  <section class="parts-overview" aria-labelledby="workflow-heading">
    <h2 id="workflow-heading">Research workflow</h2>
    <ol>
      {workflowSections.map((section) => (
        <li>
          <a href={withBase(`operations/#part-${section.id.toLowerCase()}`)}>{section.id} · {section.title}</a>
          <span>{section.summary}</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="parts-overview" aria-labelledby="supporting-content-heading">
    <h2 id="supporting-content-heading">Supporting content</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><a href={withBase('workflows/')}>Worked Workflows</a><span>Terminal-first examples backed by real case directories and bounded evidence.</span></li>
      <li><a href={withBase('tools/')}>Tools</a><span>Software and data services used by practical guides and case reconstruction.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
